.TH CHARMERA 1 "March 2026" "v0.3.2" "Charmera Companion"
.SH NAME
charmera \- AI photo organizer for keychain cameras
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B charmera
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.IR command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Charmera Companion is a photo organizer with local AI for KODAK CHARMERA and other keychain cameras.
It imports, labels, and renames photos using a local vision model (Ollama).
.PP
All processing happens locally. No cloud, no API keys, no subscriptions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBimport\fR [\fIsource\fR]
Import photos from camera or folder. Auto-detects camera if source omitted.
.TP
\fBlist\fR [\fIsource\fR]
List photos on connected camera.
.TP
\fBlabel\fR \fIphoto\fR [\fB\-m\fR \fImodel\fR]
Label a single photo using local AI. Returns description and tags.
.TP
\fBrename\fR \fIphoto\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIpattern\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
AI-label and rename a photo in one step. Default pattern: b {MM}-{DD}-{YYYY} {content}.
.TP
\fBbatch-label\fR \fIfolder\fR [\fB\-\-rename\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Label all photos in a folder. With \fB\-\-rename\fR, renames files using AI descriptions.
.TP
\fBinfo\fR \fIphoto\fR
Show photo metadata: EXIF date, dimensions, blake3 hash, camera model.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show system status: camera detection, AI models, storage location, version.
.TP
\fBdetect\fR
Check if a camera is connected.
.TP
\fBcompletions\fR \fIshell\fR
Generate shell completions (bash, zsh, fish, powershell).
.TP
\fBsplash\fR \fIphoto\fR [\fB\-\-install\fR]
Create a 960x720 boot splash screen for the camera.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output results as JSON (for AI agents and automation).
.SH NAMING PATTERN TOKENS
.TP
{MM}
Month (zero-padded)
.TP
{DD}
Day (zero-padded)
.TP
{YYYY}
Year
.TP
{content}
AI-generated description (first sentence, sanitized)
.TP
{counter}
Zero-padded sequence number
.TP
{original}
Original filename without extension
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Label a photo:
.RS
charmera label photo.jpg \-\-json
.RE
.PP
Rename all photos in a folder:
.RS
charmera batch-label ./vacation/ \-\-rename
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.charmera/catalog.db
SQLite database with photo metadata
.TP
~/.charmera/photos/
Local copies of imported photos
.TP
~/.charmera/thumbnails/
256px thumbnail cache
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ollama (1)
